Drawable Resource: 
1) First create minimum 2images in paint brush. Save at desired location. 
2) Open file explorer ,go to the desired location, copy that images and paste the images by right click on 
drawable directory under res. [i.e. app→res→drawable] in android studio. 

 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Activity_main.xml→                        app → res → drawable(folder create) ->image(put2)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?> 
<LinearLayout 
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android" 
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto" 
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools" 
    android:layout_width="match_parent" 
    android:layout_height="match_parent" 
    android:orientation="vertical" 
    tools:context=".MainActivity"> 
 
<ImageView 
        android:layout_width="wrap_content" 
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"  
        android:src="@drawable/Untitled"/> 
<ImageView 
        android:layout_width="wrap_content" 
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"  
        android:src="@drawable/Untitled1"/> 
</LinearLayout> 
 
